        "title": "Fungal Animal Pathogens",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nCANDIDA ALBICANS:\n  Commensal: lives in gut, oral cavity, vagina of ~50% of healthy adults\n  Pathogen: when host immunity weakened → opportunistic\n  Major virulence factor: DIMORPHIC SWITCH\n    Yeast form: commensal; colonizes mucosa\n    Hyphal form: invasive; tissue penetration; biofilm\n    Switch trigger: body temperature (37°C), serum, CO₂, neutral pH"
    },
