      },
      "text": "DISEASE SPECTRUM:\n  Superficial mucosal (oropharyngeal, vaginal):\n    \"Thrush\" (oral): common in infants, denture users, antibiotics, HIV\n    Vulvovaginal candidiasis: ~75% of women experience at least once\n  Deep organ / invasive:\n    Risk factors: central venous catheter, broad-spectrum antibiotics,\n      immunosuppression (neutropenia, steroids), GI surgery\n    Candidemia (bloodstream): mortality 30–45% despite treatment\n    → Biofilm on catheters → source of bloodstream infection\n    → Biofilm: resistant to fluconazole at high concentrations"
    }
